12. Saving Processed Data
Processed copies were saved separately from raw data. This preserves reproducibility and prevents the original source files from being overwritten.
os.makedirs("../data/processed", exist_ok=True)

trips_clean.to_csv(
    "../data/processed/trips_clean.csv",
    index=False
)

delivery.to_csv(
    "../data/processed/delivery_events_clean.csv",
    index=False
)
13. Why Data Quality Matters
Data quality directly affects logistics decision-making. Duplicate trips can overstate distance and fuel totals. Invalid measurements can distort fleet-efficiency KPIs. Incorrect date types can prevent accurate duration and seasonal analysis. Missing business fields can also cause incorrect classifications when their meaning is ignored. A transparent preprocessing pipeline creates a reliable foundation for predictive modeling, clustering, route analysis, and optimization.
14. Reflection
The Week 2 exercise demonstrates that cleaning is not simply deleting missing or extreme observations. Good preprocessing combines statistical methods with business context. The 124 absent termination dates were retained because they may represent active drivers, and no IQR outliers were removed because none were detected. This demonstrates that a high-quality dataset is one in which potential issues are systematically investigated and appropriate decisions are documented.
15. Conclusion
Week 2 established a reproducible data collection and preprocessing pipeline for the logistics analytics project. The data was assessed for missing values, duplicates, invalid measurements, data-type issues, and statistical outliers. The main missing-data issue was the 124 absent driver termination dates, which were retained using business interpretation. No invalid trip measurements or IQR outliers were identified in the five selected operational variables. Date fields were converted to datetime, and five numerical features were standardized successfully with means approximately equal to zero and standard deviations equal to one.
The prepared data provides a reliable foundation for Week 3 exploratory analysis of delivery performance, distance, duration, fuel efficiency, idle time, detention, routes, drivers, and fleet assets.
